{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>But we will arm ourselves swiftly.</b> Swiftly armed, as in ״מַהֵר שָׁלָל חָשׁ בַּז״ (Isaiah 8), ״יְמַהֵר יָחִישָׁה״ (ibid. 5)." "<b>Before the children of Israel.</b> At the head of the armies — because they were mighty, as it is said of Gad (Deuteronomy 33): ״וְטָרַף זְרוֹעַ אַף קָדְקֹד״. And Moses too went back and explained to them in those verses (Deuteronomy 3): ״וָאֲצַו אֶתְכֶם בָּעֵת הַהִוא וגו׳ חֲלוּצִים תַּעַבְרוּ לִפְנֵי אֲחֵיכֶם בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כָּל בְּנֵי חָיִל״, and at Jericho it is written (Joshua 6): ״וְהֶחָלוּץ עוֹבֵר (הוֹלֵךְ) לִפְנֵיהֶם״ — this is Reuben and Gad, who kept their condition." "<b>And our little ones shall dwell.</b> While we are still with our brothers." "<b>In the fortified cities.</b> That are built now."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:37.518571281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}